From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH kbase-common 003] kmod: backend ops hooks for non-DRM backends

Purpose: Extend pan_kmod with optional bo_import_fd/bo_export_fd/
 bo_mmap/bo_munmap hooks, PAN_KBASE_MAX_NODES, CSF_EVENT flag,
 pan_kmod_dev_create_with_driver() (select backend by name; kbase fd
 is not a DRM fd so drmGetVersion cannot probe it), and route
 export/mmap/munmap through the hooks.
Source/Reference: https://github.com/wonderkast02/panvk-g720-kbase-csf
 branch android-candidate-beta-1.9.4
 (src/panfrost/lib/kmod/pan_kmod.[hc]), taken verbatim: no upstream
 drift in these hunks, no arch lists touched.
Tested GPU: none yet (compile-level).
Tested Kbase UAPI: n/a.
Mesa base range: 26.3.0-devel (pinned 5a07217f).
Dependencies: 001 (HAVE_PAN_KMOD_* defines).
Validation test: build pankmod_lib with kbase; DRM backends unchanged.

